    {
      "id": 9,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Exporter Per-Source Scrape Duration",
      "description": "aether_exporter_scrape_duration_seconds per collector (a2a, t3, harness, litellm, herdr, quota). Healthy is low and flat (litellm is normally the slowest, ~0.1\u20130.2s, since it makes a real HTTP call). A step up or an outlier source means that collector is struggling (slow dependency, timeout creeping in) even while scrape_ok still reads 1.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 22
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${DS_PROMETHEUS}"
          },
          "expr": "aether_exporter_scrape_duration_seconds",
          "legendFormat": "{{source}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never"
          },
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom"
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Tracked Unrotated File Sizes",
      "description": "aether_exporter_tracked_file_bytes: current size of logs the exporter tails that nothing rotates (gateway_starts_log, a2a_audit_log, herdr_server_log). Healthy is slow, bounded growth. A steep or accelerating climb on any one file means it's heading toward filling the disk with nothing to stop it \u2014 investigate rotation for that file specifically.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 22
      },
      "datasource": {
