    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Logs \u2014 in VictoriaLogs, not here",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 28
      },
      "id": 11,
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### Logs\n\nThe fleet's journal ships to **VictoriaLogs** and is queryable at [vlogs.janpuc.com](https://vlogs.janpuc.com):\n\n```\nhost:aether AND unit:hermes-aether AND _time:1h\nhost:aether AND level:(error OR warning) AND _time:1h\n```\n\nFields on every record: `host`, `unit`, `level`, `pid`, `ident`.\n\nThere is no VictoriaLogs panel here because Grafana has no such datasource: it would need the `victoriametrics-logs-datasource` plugin, and this Grafana runs with a read-only root filesystem and `plugin_admin_enabled: false`. Adding it is a separate change to the Grafana deployment.\n\nTo read one A2A conversation rather than a log stream, use `a2a-threads show <context>` on aether."
      },
      "transparent": false
    }
  ]
}
